{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"cat work/2026-10-13-workspace-coordination/plan.md && sed -n '1,130p' work/2026-10-13-workspace-coordination/state.md && sed -n '380,447p' work/2026-10-13-workspace-coordination/state.md && cat work/2026-10-13-workspace-coordination/operations-quick.log work/2026-10-13-workspace-coordination/operations-composition.log\"","aggregated_output":"# Workspace operation coordination\n\nImplement the approved durable coordinator for concurrent development sessions.\nAgents prepare independently; brief critical sections serialize repository\nintegration and deployment activation. Waiting sessions automatically continue\nin their own Codex conversations without asking the user to resume them.\n\n## Scope and decisions\n\n- Generic scheduling, persistent job/reservation state, automatic notification,\n  merge execution, profile activation, lifecycle integration and portal status:\n  `dev-workspace`.\n- Immutable confctl deployment adapter: `vpsfree-dev-workspace`.\n- Agent procedure routing, canonical deployment target mapping, package\n  composition and rollout records: this coordination workspace.\n- Matching runtime selection and approved aitherdev deployment:\n  `vpsfree-cz-configuration`.\n- Reuse existing `codex-web` submission APIs unless precise design proves a\n  missing required capability; do not change protocol versions incidentally.\n- FIFO among ready mutations, with explicit dependencies and concurrent\n  progress for unrelated resources. Preparation, conflict resolution, review,\n  builds and long verification occur outside mutation locks.\n- A deploy-first session retains its machine reservation throughout human UI\n  review, feedback, idle turns, repeated fixes and redeployments. Only its final\n  integration and finished deployment work normally release that reservation.\n  Archive/cancel preserve unresolved deployed-state blockers.\n- Merge-only sessions work independently. Manual deployments from the build\n  machine are outside this work's scope.\n- Keep existing merge/deployment approval rules. A runtime notification never\n  supplies authorization. Material patch changes require renewed approval\n  where current procedures require it.\n- No default-branch integration is authorized by this task. Publish feature\n  branches and retain them. User explicitly authorized deployment to aitherdev\n  through vpsfree-cz-configuration; deploy without reboot and select the\n  application from its workspace user profile.\n\n## Design ownership and documentation\n\nThe user explicitly authorized GPT-6 Astra/xhigh for precise design and later\nreview. A fresh standalone designer owns `design.md`; the initiating lead\nimplements the accepted brief. A different fresh independent reviewer performs\nthe mandatory final committed-deliverable review. The tracking session is\nthreadless to avoid a second lead executing this task; it has no retained team.\nRead and retain the full applicable workspace/repository procedures.\n\nReaders are agent implementers, operators and maintainers. Keep generic feature\ncontracts and recovery documentation in dev-workspace, adapter semantics in the\nextension, site procedures here/configuration, and individual rollout evidence\nin this initiative. Register the design and other durable artifacts normally.\n\n## Compatibility and recovery\n\nUse a separately versioned private coordination journal; preserve session\nmanifest, lifecycle journal, Codex ledger and retained roster formats. Package\ntransitions must prove support for pending jobs and reservations and reject\nstale generations. Preserve forward-only profile recovery. Deterministic\nmutation workers must survive coordinator/portal restarts, and unknown mutation\noutcomes must be reconciled before retry or resource release.\n\nNo application database, client API or vpsAdminOS node protocol changes are\nintended. No coordinated update of running nodes is required. Browser/terminal\nclients retain the selected validated Codex protocol. Establish bootstrap,\nupgrade, generation checks, schema failure and recovery semantics in design.\n\n## Verification and rollout\n\nVerify concurrent merges with stale-baseline refresh; short critical sections\ndespite slow preparation; concurrent unrelated resources; repeated deploy-first\niteration and cumulative later deployments; merge-only jobs; automatic wakeup;\ndelivery/execution interruption; approval/ownership/cancellation/lifecycle and\npackage compatibility. Use repository Nix environments. Quick checks precede\nthe final independent review; long VM/App Server tests, CI and builds follow it\nand use fresh Luna/low verification watchers. Preserve session continuity in the\napproved no-reboot aitherdev rollout. Run the workspace/configuration deployment\ncontract check and retain exact sources, live identities and recovery evidence.\n---\nlifecycle: active\n---\n\n# Workspace operation coordination\n\nPhase: implementing the approved Operations subpage and reservation badges.\nThe previous candidate remains deployed and live-verified on aitherdev.\nFeature branches are ready, awaiting merge approval. The initiative stays active\nand owns vpsfree:aitherdev throughout review, feedback and iteration.\n\nThe exact final application and matching system are selected (profile-118 and\nsystem-190). Both independent activation workers exited 0. Boot ID, running\nkernel and Codex/provider PIDs are unchanged; coordinator, router and portal are\nactive. Portal/Operations API checks pass and show both completed jobs. See\n[rollout.md](rollout.md) and [deployed-live-acceptance.json](deployed-live-acceptance.json).\n\n## Phase checklist\n\nPresentation follow-up: implementation, quick checks, affected independent review,\nsuccessor package verification and reserved no-reboot redeployment are pending.\nThe accepted brief is appended to design.md. The initiating lead owns this bounded\nUI/status change; no team roster or native lead thread exists. The retained\nindependent Astra/xhigh reviewer will assess the completed committed change.\n\nOperations implementation now complete: dedicated /operations menu/page,\nmachine-only badges from an incarnation-matched untruncated portal projection,\nfive-second visible-only reads and failed-read retention. Focused checks pass:\nNode browser regressions 3/3; Ruby portal projection 3/27; Go Operations and\nAutomatic archival route checks pass. Full log operations-quick.log. Two initial\nfixture failures are preserved separately: sorted ledger UUIDs invalidated the\nhistory-order assumption (fixed deterministic fixture IDs), and the host's real\nprovider catalog affected unregistered Go fixtures (isolated with the supported\nDEV_WORKSPACES_CODEX_PROVIDERS override). README documents the focused-test setup.\nNo runtime activation or persistent ledger mutation was performed by these checks.\n\n- [x] User-approved behavior and aitherdev deployment target established.\n- [x] Dedicated threadless initiative created from the initiating conversation.\n- [x] Precise Astra/xhigh design and verification brief accepted.\n- [x] Implementation and project documentation complete.\n- [x] Quick local checks and complete feature history inventory pass.\n- [x] Independent original final review complete and findings reconciled.\n- [x] Independent confctl initialization follow-up review complete.\n- [x] Original longer integration checks and exact branch CI pass.\n- [x] Revised extension CI and previous composed candidate pass.\n- [x] Runtime JSON-output correction reviewed; new exact package and CI pass.\n- [x] Approved aitherdev rollout and live acceptance checks complete.\n- [ ] User deployed review, feedback and any iterations complete.\n- [ ] Feature integration explicitly approved and final heads merged.\n\n## Current summary\n\nAll final checks passed: independent Astra/xhigh review (including complete\nhistories and no migrations), exact runtime/extension CI, composed package checks,\nmatching system build and deployment composition. Published heads are runtime\n0651f64c, extension c697acc7, workspace 09156337 and configuration 63a0b59a.\nAll four worktrees are clean and retain two consolidated feature commits each.\n\nFinal preparation passed in workspace-coordination-bootstrap-prepare-20261013-stdout.service\n(invocation b7b3eb5f2b0d4cba9eb7b3e11e9deb77). Request\na0caa52d-042b-4640-9379-cf47553370f7 retains the exact machine/profile artifacts\nand clean workspace source. Execution preflight independently verified all frozen\nevidence checksums, source heads, predecessor token and unchanged live identities;\nexecution-preflight-live.json records the observation. The ledger has one\nthreadless owner and no jobs/reservations/approvals; nothing has activated yet.\n\nExecution completed successfully in workspace-coordination-bootstrap-execute-20261013.service,\ninvocation 6f1db5c58e6345b3b9de2924fe90c047, using the exact returned request.\nMachine job 03a23921-56de-4dcc-8514-b33c018b1caf and dependent profile job\nb4a9c19a-39fd-4a4d-9f70-8f0e78ee4c22 both succeeded. Live acceptance passed;\ndeployed-live-acceptance.json binds their exact workers, results and checksums.\n\nReservation d114323d-806c-479f-b7a4-8c1a08afb45b remains deployed_review for\nvpsfree:aitherdev. Its threadless bootstrap owner is\n55e83d75-cb96-417a-9308-11d3caf22dcd. For read-only status use both verified\nenvironment identity values and:\n`dev-session coordination status 2026-10-13-workspace-coordination --as-is --json\n--bootstrap-owner 55e83d75-cb96-417a-9308-11d3caf22dcd`.\n\nNext: user review through the stable portal, then address feedback while retaining\nthe reservation. Default-branch integration still requires explicit direction for\nthe four repository/target pairs. Finish/release also requires integration proof\nand explicit deployment/review completion; do not run it now. 